From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:16:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: wch,ch334: Allow hard wired devices on the
 ports

The CH334 hub node is used for hubs with a soldered device on a port.
usb-hub.yaml already allows such child nodes, but additionalProperties
rejects them. Use unevaluatedProperties as the other hub bindings do.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with a device tree that
uses this binding; the hub node with its device child binds and
dtbs_check reports nothing.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/wch,ch334.yaml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/wch,ch334.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/wch,ch334.yaml
index 2fdca14dc1de..1dd7d36d9bd5 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/wch,ch334.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/wch,ch334.yaml
@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@ required:
   - compatible
   - reg
 
-additionalProperties: false
+unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
